// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/dark-mode-switch.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeDarkModeSwitch(path: "/recipes/dark-mode-switch", title: "Add a dark-mode switch — Recipes", description: "Let the reader pick light, dark or the system's choice with setTheme, and mark the current choice by reading theme.") {
    RecipeShell("Add a dark-mode switch", summary: "Let the reader pick a light look, a dark one, or whatever their system prefers, and keep that choice across visits. The switch needs a dark theme named in `webfluent.app.json`:", outputs: ["website", "app", "desktop"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Add a picture, sized for every screen", to: "/recipes/add-a-picture"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Add video and audio", to: "/recipes/video-and-audio"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Show an icon", to: "/recipes/show-an-icon")], source: "md-docs/recipes/dark-mode-switch.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** the `theme` setting below in `webfluent.app.json`. The starter already declares `theme Night` in `src/theme.wf` and a `ThemeToggle` component that does this; replace `src/theme.wf` with this code's themes, and its `Settings` page replaces the starter's `src/pages/Settings.wf`.")
            CodeBlock(#"{ "theme": { "name": "Light", "dark": "Night" } }"#, title: "json")
            Markdown("This program declares both themes and a settings page with three buttons, the current choice drawn solid and the others outlined:")
            CodeBlock(#"theme Light {
    color-background: #FFFFFF
    color-text: #0F172A
}

theme Night {
    color-background: #0B1220
    color-surface: #111827
    color-text: #E5E7EB
    color-text-muted: #9CA3AF
    color-border: #1F2937
}

page Settings(path: "/settings", title: "Settings", description: "How the site looks.") {
    Heading("Settings").h1
    Row(gap: .sm) {
        Button("Light", outlined: theme != "light") { on click { setTheme("light") } }
        Button("Dark", outlined: theme != "dark") { on click { setTheme("dark") } }
        Button("Match the system", outlined: theme != "system") { on click { setTheme("system") } }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("- **Two themes.** `Night` names only the tokens that change in the dark; every token it leaves out keeps its value. The config's `theme.dark` says which theme is the dark one ([Styling](/learn/13-styling#dark-mode)).\n- **`setTheme`** takes `\"light\"`, `\"dark\"` or `\"system\"`, and the choice is kept across visits. With `\"system\"`, the dark theme applies whenever the reader's system prefers dark (`prefers-color-scheme: dark`).\n- **`theme`** reads the choice, and stays current. A `Bool` prop given a condition follows it, so `outlined: theme != \"light\"` outlines every button but the chosen one.")

    }
}
